@ENUM
.
=ENUM
.
.ENUM name ... END ENUM makes a set of named constants, the members. ENDENUM
.is the same as END ENUM. A line holds one member, or several separated by
.commas.
.
:ENUM STATE
:  READY, RUNNING
:  BLOCKED = 10
:  DONE             ' 11
:  LAST = DONE + 5
:END ENUM
:PRINT STATE.READY; STATE.RUNNING; STATE.BLOCKED; STATE.DONE; STATE.LAST
.
.This prints 0 1 10 11 16.
.
.  - Members number from 0. NAME = value sets a member's number, and the
.    members after it count on by 1. The value is a constant expression, and
.    can use an earlier member bare and any CONST.
.  - Inside the ENUM a member is used bare, in a value only. Outside it is
.    qualified: STATE.READY. An ENUM MODE in namespace GFX gives
.    GFX.MODE.TEXT.
.  - The members are UBYTE when every value is 0 to 255. When one passes 255,
.    the ENUM and every member are UWORD.
.  - A member is a constant. It takes no RAM and no space in the PRG.
.  - A member name takes no mark. A $ is a syntax error. A % stops the
.    compile with % IS NOT A MARK: USE AS UWORD.
.  - An ENUM may be in a namespace or a SUB.
.  - Errors: ENUM WITHOUT END ENUM at the ENUM's line when the source ends
.    inside it, END ENUM WITHOUT ENUM, TOO BIG FOR A WORD: name for a count
.    past 65535, VALUE NOT A CONSTANT.
.
.See CONST, Namespaces, Types.
.
